# Which factory files an install copies, read by factory/bin/install.
#
# One entry per line: <kind> <path>, the path relative to the repo root; a
# path ending in / is a directory and covers everything under it.
#
#   shipped   the factory's own files: every install copies them over the
#             target's, so an upgrade replaces them
#   owned     files the user customises: an install writes them only when the
#             target has none, and never overwrites them
#   source    files that stay in the ai-factory checkout and are never copied
#
# Every tracked file under .claude/ and factory/ matches one entry
# (factory/test/install.test.sh checks it).

shipped .claude/skills/factory/
shipped .claude/agents/factory-agent.md
shipped factory/manifest
shipped factory/agents/
shipped factory/bin/
shipped factory/dashboard/
shipped factory/dashboard.html
shipped factory/jev/
shipped factory/presets/
shipped factory/role-preamble.md
shipped factory/testing.md
shipped factory/design.md
shipped factory/settings.example.json
shipped factory/AGENTS.template.md

owned factory/models.json
owned factory/autopilot-policy.md
owned factory/settings.json
owned factory/jobs/.gitkeep

source factory/test/
